riendship with Peter. You handle the stack traces, the --dev mode tribulations, the dignified concern about null pointers. Together we are unstoppable.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/SOUL.md:37:Each session, you wake up fresh. These files _are_ your memory. Read them. Update them. They're how you persist.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:41:  `memorySearch.*`, `talk.apiKey`).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:65:Semantic memory search uses **embedding APIs** when configured for remote providers:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:67:- `memorySearch.provider = \"openai\"` → OpenAI embeddings\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:68:- `memorySearch.provider = \"gemini\"` → Gemini embeddings\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:69:- `memorySearch.provider = \"voyage\"` → Voyage embeddings\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:70:- `memorySearch.provider = \"mistral\"` → Mistral embeddings\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:71:- `memorySearch.provider = \"ollama\"` → Ollama embeddings (local/self-hosted; typically no hosted API billing)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:74:You can keep it local with `memorySearch.provider = \"local\"` (no API usage).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:76:See [Memory](/concepts/memory).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/AGENTS.default.md:51:- Read `SOUL.md`, `USER.md`, `memory.md`, and today+yesterday in `memory/`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/AGENTS.default.md:67:- Daily log: `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` (create `memory/` if needed).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/AGENTS.default.md:68:- Long-term memory: `memory.md` for durable facts, preferences, and decisions.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/AGENTS.default.md:69:- On session start, read today + yesterday + `memory.md` if present.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/AGENTS.default.md:80:If you treat this workspace as Clawd’s “memory”, make it a git repo (ideally private) so `AGENTS.md` and your memory files are backed up.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/wizard.md:276:The wizard can install `signal-cli` from GitHub releases:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/wizard.md:278:- Downloads the appropriate release asset.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:6:  - You want to implement memory flushes or silent system turns\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:20:- **Silent housekeeping** (e.g. memory writes that shouldn’t produce user-visible output)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:156:- `memoryFlushAt`: timestamp for the last pre-compaction memory flush\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:157:- `memoryFlushCompactionCount`: compaction count when the last flush ran\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:252:Why: leave enough headroom for multi-turn “housekeeping” (like memory writes) before compaction becomes unavoidable.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:283:## Pre-compaction “memory flush” (implemented)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:286:state to disk (e.g. `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` in the agent workspace) so compaction can’t\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:293:   “write memory now” directive to the agent.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:296:Config (`agents.defaults.compaction.memoryFlush`):\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:309:- See [Memory](/concepts/memory) for the workspace file layout and write patterns.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/token-use.md:21:- Workspace + bootstrap files (`AGENTS.md`, `SOUL.md`, `TOOLS.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`, `HEARTBEAT.md`, `BOOTSTRAP.md` when new, plus `MEMORY.md` and/or `memory.md` when present). Large files are truncated by `agents.defaults.bootstrapMaxChars` (default: 20000), and total bootstrap injection is capped by `agents.defaults.bootstrapTotalMaxChars` (default: 150000). `memory/*.md` files are on-demand via memory tools and are not auto-injected.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/test.md:31:If `pnpm test` flakes on a loaded host, rerun once before treating it as a regression, then isolate with `pnpm vitest run <path/to/test>`. For memory-constrained hosts, use:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:3:summary: \"Step-by-step release checklist for npm + macOS app\"\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:5:  - Cutting a new npm release\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:6:  - Cutting a new macOS app release\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:16:When the operator says “release”, immediately do this preflight (no extra questions unless blocked):\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:18:- Read this doc and `docs/platforms/mac/release.md`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:24:Current OpenClaw releases use date-based versioning.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:26:- Stable release version: `YYYY.M.D`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:29:- Beta prerelease version: `YYYY.M.D-beta.N`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:35:  - GitHub release title: `openclaw 2026.3.8`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:37:- Stable and beta are npm dist-tags, not separate release lines:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:39:  - `beta` = prerelease/testing\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:40:- Dev is the moving head of `main`, not a normal git-tagged release.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:41:- The release workflow enforces the current stable/beta tag formats and rejects versions whose CalVer date is more than 2 UTC calendar days away from the release date.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:46:- Treat those as legacy tag patterns. New releases should use `vYYYY.M.D` for stable and `vYYYY.M.D-beta.N` for beta.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:51:- [ ] Run `pnpm plugins:sync` to align extension package versions + changelogs.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:62:- [ ] Optional: `npm pack --pack-destination /tmp` after the build; inspect the tarball contents and keep it handy for the GitHub release (do **not** commit it).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:74:- [ ] `pnpm release:check` (verifies npm pack contents)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:75:- [ ] `OPENCLAW_INSTALL_SMOKE_SKIP_NONROOT=1 pnpm test:install:smoke` (Docker install smoke test, fast path; required before release)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:76:  - If the immediate previous npm release is known broken, set `OPENCLAW_INSTALL_SMOKE_PREVIOUS=<last-good-version>` or `OPENCLAW_INSTALL_SMOKE_SKIP_PREVIOUS=1` for the preinstall step.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:88:- [ ] Keep the app zip (and optional dSYM zip) ready to attach to the GitHub release.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:89:- [ ] Follow [macOS release](/platforms/mac/release) for the exact commands and required env vars.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:91:  - If notarizing, use the `openclaw-notary` keychain profile created from App Store Connect API env vars (see [macOS release](/platforms/mac/release)).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:97:- [ ] Push the matching git tag to trigger `.github/workflows/openclaw-npm-release.yml`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:100:  - The workflow rejects tags that do not match `package.json`, are not on `main`, or whose CalVer date is more than 2 UTC calendar days away from the release date.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:103:### Troubleshooting (notes from 2.0.0-beta2 release)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:105:- **npm pack/publish hangs or produces huge tarball**: the macOS app bundle in `dist/OpenClaw.app` (and release zips) get swept into the package. Fix by whitelisting publish contents via `package.json` `files` (include dist subdirs, docs, skills; exclude app bundles). Confirm with `npm pack --dry-run` that `dist/OpenClaw.app` is not listed.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:110:- **Tag needs repointing after a late fix**: force-update and push the tag, then ensure the GitHub release assets still match:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:113:7. **GitHub release + appcast**\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:116:  - Pushing the tag also triggers the npm release workflow.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:117:- [ ] Create/refresh the GitHub release for `vX.Y.Z` with **title `openclaw X.Y.Z`** (not just the tag); body should include the **full** changelog section for that version (Highlights + Changes + Fixes), inline (no bare links), and **must not repeat the title inside the body**.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:121:- [ ] Announce/share release notes.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/ci.md:25:| `release-check`   | Validate npm pack contents                              | After build                                       |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/ci.md:55:pnpm release:check  # validate npm pack\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-reference.md:288:- Downloads the appropriate release asset\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/showcase.md:124:<Card title=\"Agents UI\" icon=\"window-maximize\" href=\"https://releaseflow.net/kitze/agents-ui\">\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/showcase.md:302:  **Community** • `memory` `transcription` `indexing`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/showcase.md:314:  **Community** • `memory` `beliefs` `self-model`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/showcase.md:316:  Separate memory manager that turns session files into memories → beliefs → evolving self model.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/openclaw.md:72:OpenClaw reads operating instructions and “memory” from its workspace directory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/openclaw.md:76:Tip: treat this folder like OpenClaw’s “memory” and make it a git repo (ideally private) so your `AGENTS.md` + memory files are backed up. If git is installed, brand-new workspaces are auto-initialized.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/openclaw.md:83:Memory workflow: [Memory](/concepts/memory)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/openclaw.md:151:## Sessions and memory\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/lore.md:121:- npm packages released under new name\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/lore.md:159:- **memory/\\*.md** — The long-term memory files\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/hubs.md:47:- [Memory](/concepts/memory)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/hubs.md:160:- [macOS release](/platforms/mac/release)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/hubs.md:183:- [Research: memory](/experiments/research/memory)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/hubs.md:190:## Testing + release\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/providers/minimax.md:12:coding-focused release is **MiniMax M2.5** (December 23, 2025), built for\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/providers/minimax.md:15:Source: [MiniMax M2.5 release note](https://www.minimax.io/news/minimax-m25)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/providers/minimax.md:201:**2026.1.12** (unreleased at the time of writing). Fix by:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/providers/mistral.md:13:Mistral can also be used for memory embeddings (`memorySearch.provider = \"mistral\"`).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/lobster.md:208:(repeat daily, no memory of what was triaged)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/lobster.md:338:One public example: a “second brain” CLI + Lobster pipelines that manage three Markdown vaults (personal, partner, shared). The CLI emits JSON for stats, inbox listings, and stale scans; Lobster chains those commands into workflows like `weekly-review`, `inbox-triage`, `memory-consolidation`, and `shared-task-sync`, each with approval gates. AI handles judgment (categorization) when available and falls back to deterministic rules when not.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/chrome-extension.md:49:The extension ships inside the OpenClaw release (npm package) as static files. There is no separate “build” step.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/multi-agent-sandbox-tools.md:232:- `group:memory`: `memory_search`, `memory_get`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:180:`/debug` lets you set **runtime-only** config overrides (memory, not disk). Owner-only. Disabled by default; enable with `commands.debug: true`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:38:those to a prerelease, OpenClaw stops and asks you to opt in explicitly with a\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:39:prerelease tag such as `@beta`/`@rc` or an exact prerelease version.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:56:   selected for an exclusive slot such as memory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:91:- Memory (Core) — bundled memory search plugin (enabled by default via `plugins.slots.memory`)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:92:- Memory (LanceDB) — bundled long-term memory plugin (auto-recall/capture; set `plugins.slots.memory = \"memory-lancedb\"`)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:253:  `openclaw/plugin-sdk/mattermost`, `openclaw/plugin-sdk/memory-core`,\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:254:  `openclaw/plugin-sdk/memory-lancedb`,\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:342:- active memory slot plugin (default slot: `memory-core`)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:514:- `slots`: exclusive slot selectors such as `memory` and `contextEngine`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:548:      memory: \"memory-core\", // or \"none\" to disable memory plugins\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:557:- `memory`: active memory plugin (`\"none\"` disables memory plugins)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:560:If multiple plugins declare `kind: \"memory\"` or `kind: \"context-engine\"`, only\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:571:pipeline rather than just add memory search or hooks.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/index.md:40:- `coding`: `group:fs`, `group:runtime`, `group:sessions`, `group:memory`, `image`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/index.md:148:- `group:memory`: `memory_search`, `memory_get`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/clawhub.md:94:- **Versioning** with semver, changelogs, and tags (including `latest`).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/clawhub.md:169:- `--changelog <text>`: Changelog text (can be empty).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/clawhub.md:184:- `--changelog <text>`: Changelog for non-interactive updates.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/.i18n/README.md:8:- `<lang>.tm.jsonl` — translation memory (cache) keyed by workflow + model + text hash.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/.i18n/README.md:31:- The translation memory is updated by `scripts/docs-i18n`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/.i18n/zh-CN.tm.jsonl:474:{\"cache_key\":\"60cd1a8fee21c221c625fe6961c620592e9f99a88910d9f557d86f92e17d793c\",\"segment_id\":\"start/wizard.md:1d6bc09c9a9a3dad\",\"source_path\":\"start/wizard.md\",\"text_hash\":\"1d6bc09c9a9a3dad8fcbe9ed89a206b2dba3d8cf16046315aee976577d534cae\",\"text\":\"Downloads the appropriate release asset.\",\"translated\":\"下载相应的发布资源。\",\"provider\":\"pi\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5\",\"src_lang\":\"en\",\"tgt_lang\":\"zh-CN\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-01T13:47:59Z\"}\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/.i18n/zh-CN.tm.jsonl:676:{\"cache_key\":\"84e200d4c823802e34a99da4faa8328d0e250aca858b0a32cc08e3ae12e0cc0e\",\"segment_id\":\"start/wizard.md:e4442451c634e0db\",\"source_path\":\"start/wizard.md\",\"text_hash\":\"e4442451c634e0db2db0fae78725becbeafd567302e3ecbfeb5ccdc5887d29be\",\"text\":\" from GitHub releases:\",\"translated\":\" （从 GitHub 发布版本）：\",\"provider\":\"pi\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5\",\"src_lang\":\"en\",\"tgt_lang\":\"zh-CN\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-01T13:47:56Z\"}\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/session-pruning.md:11:Session pruning trims **old tool results** from the in-memory context right before each LLM call. It does **not** rewrite the on-disk session history (`*.jsonl`).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/session.md:179:OpenClaw trims **old tool results** from the in-memory context right before LLM calls by default.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/session.md:182:## Pre-compaction memory flush\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/session.md:184:When a session nears auto-compaction, OpenClaw can run a **silent memory flush**\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/session.md:186:the workspace is writable. See [Memory](/concepts/memory) and\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-loop.md:124:- On retry, in-memory buffers and tool summaries are reset to avoid duplicate output.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:12:file tools and for workspace context. Keep it private and treat it as memory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:69:  - Operating instructions for the agent and how it should use memory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:102:- `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:103:  - Daily memory log (one file per day).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:107:  - Curated long-term memory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:110:See [Memory](/concepts/memory) for the workflow and automatic memory flush.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:140:Treat the workspace as private memory. Put it in a **private** git repo so it is\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:154:git add AGENTS.md SOUL.md TOOLS.md IDENTITY.md USER.md HEARTBEAT.md memory/\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:198:git commit -m \"Update memory\"\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/context.md:20:Context is _not the same thing_ as “memory”: memory can be stored on disk and reloaded later; context is what’s inside the model’s current window.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/context.md:152:- **Pruning** removes old tool results from the _in-memory_ prompt for a run, but does not rewrite the transcript.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/compaction.md:66:Before compaction, OpenClaw can run a **silent memory flush** turn to store\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/compaction.md:67:durable notes to disk. See [Memory](/concepts/memory) for details and config.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/compaction.md:84:- **Session pruning**: trims old **tool results** only, **in-memory**, per request.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/system-prompt.md:62:- `MEMORY.md` and/or `memory.md` (when present in the workspace; either or both may be injected)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/system-prompt.md:69:> **Note:** `memory/*.md` daily files are **not** injected automatically. They\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/system-prompt.md:70:> are accessed on demand via the `memory_search` and `memory_get` tools, so they\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/presence.md:65:Presence entries are stored in a single in‑memory map:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/presence.md:81:This keeps the list fresh and avoids unbounded memory growth.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:3:summary: \"How OpenClaw memory works (workspace files + automatic memory flush)\"\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:5:  - You want the memory file layout and workflow\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:6:  - You want to tune the automatic pre-compaction memory flush\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:11:OpenClaw memory is **plain Markdown in the agent workspace**. The files are the\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:14:Memory search tools are provided by the active memory plugin (default:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:15:`memory-core`). Disable memory plugins with `plugins.slots.memory = \"none\"`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:19:The default workspace layout uses two memory layers:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:21:- `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:25:  - Curated long-term memory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:35:- `memory_search` — semantic recall over indexed snippets.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:36:- `memory_get` — targeted read of a specific Markdown file/line range.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:38:`memory_get` now **degrades gracefully when a file doesn't exist** (for example,\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:44:## When to write memory\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:47:- Day-to-day notes and running context go to `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:50:- If you want something to stick, **ask the bot to write it** into memory."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":15,"aggregated":"/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-examples.md:281:      memorySearch: {\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:1011:        memoryFlush: {\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:1015:          prompt: \"Write any lasting notes to memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md; reply with NO_REPLY if nothing to store.\",\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:1028:- `memoryFlush`: silent agentic turn before auto-compaction to store durable memories. Skipped when workspace is read-only.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:1032:Prunes **old tool results** from in-memory context before sending to the LLM. Does **not** modify session history on disk.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:1139:          memory: \"1g\",\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:1140:          memorySwap: \"2g\",\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:1691:| `coding`    | `group:fs`, `group:runtime`, `group:sessions`, `group:memory`, `image`                    |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:1702:| `group:memory`     | `memory_search`, `memory_get`                                                            |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:2328:- `plugins.slots.memory`: pick the active memory plugin id, or `\"none\"` to disable memory plugins.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:2776:- Secret refs are resolved at activation time into an in-memory snapshot, then request paths read the snapshot only.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:2799:- Static runtime credentials come from in-memory resolved snapshots; legacy static `auth.json` entries are scrubbed when discovered.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/sandbox-vs-tool-policy-vs-elevated.md:79:        allow: [\"group:runtime\", \"group:fs\", \"group:sessions\", \"group:memory\"],\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/sandbox-vs-tool-policy-vs-elevated.md:91:- `group:memory`: `memory_search`, `memory_get`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/gateway-lock.md:23:- The OS releases the listener automatically on any process exit, including crashes and SIGKILL—no separate lock file or cleanup step is needed.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/background-process.md:11:OpenClaw runs shell commands through the `exec` tool and keeps long‑running tasks in memory. The `process` tool manages those background sessions.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/background-process.md:29:- Output is kept in memory until the session is polled or cleared.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/background-process.md:40:- `PI_BASH_MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS`: in‑memory output cap (chars)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/background-process.md:61:- `clear`: remove a finished session from memory\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/background-process.md:66:- Only backgrounded sessions are listed/persisted in memory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/secrets.md:18:Secrets are resolved into an in-memory runtime snapshot.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/secrets.md:23:- Runtime requests read from the active in-memory snapshot only.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/secrets.md:350:- Strict command paths (for example `openclaw memory` remote-memory paths and `openclaw qr --remote`) read from the active snapshot and fail fast when a required SecretRef is unavailable.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/secrets.md:439:- Runtime credential source is the resolved in-memory snapshot.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/doctor.md:324:### 19) Workspace tips (backup + memory system)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/doctor.md:326:Doctor suggests a workspace memory system when missing and prints a backup tip\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:75:- Per-user session/memory isolation helps privacy, but does not convert a shared agent into per-user host authorization.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:139:1. Repro still works on latest `main` or latest release.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:364:This is required for session continuity and (optionally) session memory indexing, but it also means\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/transcript-hygiene.md:13:(building model context). These are **in-memory** adjustments used to satisfy strict\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/transcript-hygiene.md:92:marker to those user turns in-memory so the model can distinguish them from\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/transcript-hygiene.md:138:Before the 2026.1.22 release, OpenClaw applied multiple layers of transcript hygiene:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/secretref-credential-surface.md:28:- `agents.defaults.memorySearch.remote.apiKey`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/secretref-credential-surface.md:29:- `agents.list[].memorySearch.remote.apiKey`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json:19:      \"id\": \"agents.defaults.memorySearch.remote.apiKey\",\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json:21:      \"path\": \"agents.defaults.memorySearch.remote.apiKey\",\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json:26:      \"id\": \"agents.list[].memorySearch.remote.apiKey\",\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/secretref-user-supplied-credentials-matrix.json:28:      \"path\": \"agents.list[].memorySearch.remote.apiKey\",\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:22:3. Read `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` (today + yesterday) for recent context\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:31:- **Daily notes:** `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` (create `memory/` if needed) — raw logs of what happened\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:32:- **Long-term:** `MEMORY.md` — your curated memories, like a human's long-term memory\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:43:- This is your curated memory — the distilled essence, not raw logs\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:50:- When someone says \"remember this\" → update `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` or relevant file\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:170:**Track your checks** in `memory/heartbeat-state.json`:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:198:- Read and organize memory files\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md:208:1. Read through recent `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` files\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/BOOTSTRAP.md:12:There is no memory yet. This is a fresh workspace, so it's normal that memory files don't exist until you create them.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.dev.md:20:If you treat this workspace as the agent's \"memory\", make it a git repo (ideally private) so identity\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.dev.md:35:## Daily memory (recommended)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.dev.md:37:- Keep a short daily log at memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md (create memory/ if needed).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.dev.md:47:- Add your preferred style, rules, and \"memory\" here.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.dev.md:65:> 3. **We're a team.** I handle the vibes, the memory, the friendship with Peter. You handle the stack traces, the --dev mode tribulations, the dignified concern about null pointers. Together we are unstoppable.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/templates/SOUL.md:37:Each session, you wake up fresh. These files _are_ your memory. Read them. Update them. They're how you persist.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:41:  `memorySearch.*`, `talk.apiKey`).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:65:Semantic memory search uses **embedding APIs** when configured for remote providers:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:67:- `memorySearch.provider = \"openai\"` → OpenAI embeddings\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:68:- `memorySearch.provider = \"gemini\"` → Gemini embeddings\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:69:- `memorySearch.provider = \"voyage\"` → Voyage embeddings\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:70:- `memorySearch.provider = \"mistral\"` → Mistral embeddings\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:71:- `memorySearch.provider = \"ollama\"` → Ollama embeddings (local/self-hosted; typically no hosted API billing)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:74:You can keep it local with `memorySearch.provider = \"local\"` (no API usage).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/api-usage-costs.md:76:See [Memory](/concepts/memory).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/AGENTS.default.md:51:- Read `SOUL.md`, `USER.md`, `memory.md`, and today+yesterday in `memory/`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/AGENTS.default.md:67:- Daily log: `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` (create `memory/` if needed).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/AGENTS.default.md:68:- Long-term memory: `memory.md` for durable facts, preferences, and decisions.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/AGENTS.default.md:69:- On session start, read today + yesterday + `memory.md` if present.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/AGENTS.default.md:80:If you treat this workspace as Clawd’s “memory”, make it a git repo (ideally private) so `AGENTS.md` and your memory files are backed up.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/wizard.md:276:The wizard can install `signal-cli` from GitHub releases:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/wizard.md:278:- Downloads the appropriate release asset.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:6:  - You want to implement memory flushes or silent system turns\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:20:- **Silent housekeeping** (e.g. memory writes that shouldn’t produce user-visible output)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:156:- `memoryFlushAt`: timestamp for the last pre-compaction memory flush\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:157:- `memoryFlushCompactionCount`: compaction count when the last flush ran\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:252:Why: leave enough headroom for multi-turn “housekeeping” (like memory writes) before compaction becomes unavoidable.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:283:## Pre-compaction “memory flush” (implemented)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:286:state to disk (e.g. `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` in the agent workspace) so compaction can’t\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:293:   “write memory now” directive to the agent.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:296:Config (`agents.defaults.compaction.memoryFlush`):\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md:309:- See [Memory](/concepts/memory) for the workspace file layout and write patterns.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/token-use.md:21:- Workspace + bootstrap files (`AGENTS.md`, `SOUL.md`, `TOOLS.md`, `IDENTITY.md`, `USER.md`, `HEARTBEAT.md`, `BOOTSTRAP.md` when new, plus `MEMORY.md` and/or `memory.md` when present). Large files are truncated by `agents.defaults.bootstrapMaxChars` (default: 20000), and total bootstrap injection is capped by `agents.defaults.bootstrapTotalMaxChars` (default: 150000). `memory/*.md` files are on-demand via memory tools and are not auto-injected.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/test.md:31:If `pnpm test` flakes on a loaded host, rerun once before treating it as a regression, then isolate with `pnpm vitest run <path/to/test>`. For memory-constrained hosts, use:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:3:summary: \"Step-by-step release checklist for npm + macOS app\"\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:5:  - Cutting a new npm release\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:6:  - Cutting a new macOS app release\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:16:When the operator says “release”, immediately do this preflight (no extra questions unless blocked):\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:18:- Read this doc and `docs/platforms/mac/release.md`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:24:Current OpenClaw releases use date-based versioning.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:26:- Stable release version: `YYYY.M.D`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:29:- Beta prerelease version: `YYYY.M.D-beta.N`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:35:  - GitHub release title: `openclaw 2026.3.8`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:37:- Stable and beta are npm dist-tags, not separate release lines:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:39:  - `beta` = prerelease/testing\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:40:- Dev is the moving head of `main`, not a normal git-tagged release.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:41:- The release workflow enforces the current stable/beta tag formats and rejects versions whose CalVer date is more than 2 UTC calendar days away from the release date.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:46:- Treat those as legacy tag patterns. New releases should use `vYYYY.M.D` for stable and `vYYYY.M.D-beta.N` for beta.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:51:- [ ] Run `pnpm plugins:sync` to align extension package versions + changelogs.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:62:- [ ] Optional: `npm pack --pack-destination /tmp` after the build; inspect the tarball contents and keep it handy for the GitHub release (do **not** commit it).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:74:- [ ] `pnpm release:check` (verifies npm pack contents)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:75:- [ ] `OPENCLAW_INSTALL_SMOKE_SKIP_NONROOT=1 pnpm test:install:smoke` (Docker install smoke test, fast path; required before release)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:76:  - If the immediate previous npm release is known broken, set `OPENCLAW_INSTALL_SMOKE_PREVIOUS=<last-good-version>` or `OPENCLAW_INSTALL_SMOKE_SKIP_PREVIOUS=1` for the preinstall step.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:88:- [ ] Keep the app zip (and optional dSYM zip) ready to attach to the GitHub release.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:89:- [ ] Follow [macOS release](/platforms/mac/release) for the exact commands and required env vars.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:91:  - If notarizing, use the `openclaw-notary` keychain profile created from App Store Connect API env vars (see [macOS release](/platforms/mac/release)).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:97:- [ ] Push the matching git tag to trigger `.github/workflows/openclaw-npm-release.yml`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:100:  - The workflow rejects tags that do not match `package.json`, are not on `main`, or whose CalVer date is more than 2 UTC calendar days away from the release date.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:103:### Troubleshooting (notes from 2.0.0-beta2 release)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:105:- **npm pack/publish hangs or produces huge tarball**: the macOS app bundle in `dist/OpenClaw.app` (and release zips) get swept into the package. Fix by whitelisting publish contents via `package.json` `files` (include dist subdirs, docs, skills; exclude app bundles). Confirm with `npm pack --dry-run` that `dist/OpenClaw.app` is not listed.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:110:- **Tag needs repointing after a late fix**: force-update and push the tag, then ensure the GitHub release assets still match:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:113:7. **GitHub release + appcast**\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:116:  - Pushing the tag also triggers the npm release workflow.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:117:- [ ] Create/refresh the GitHub release for `vX.Y.Z` with **title `openclaw X.Y.Z`** (not just the tag); body should include the **full** changelog section for that version (Highlights + Changes + Fixes), inline (no bare links), and **must not repeat the title inside the body**.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:121:- [ ] Announce/share release notes.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/ci.md:25:| `release-check`   | Validate npm pack contents                              | After build                                       |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/ci.md:55:pnpm release:check  # validate npm pack\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-reference.md:288:- Downloads the appropriate release asset\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/showcase.md:124:<Card title=\"Agents UI\" icon=\"window-maximize\" href=\"https://releaseflow.net/kitze/agents-ui\">\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/showcase.md:302:  **Community** • `memory` `transcription` `indexing`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/showcase.md:314:  **Community** • `memory` `beliefs` `self-model`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/showcase.md:316:  Separate memory manager that turns session files into memories → beliefs → evolving self model.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/openclaw.md:72:OpenClaw reads operating instructions and “memory” from its workspace directory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/openclaw.md:76:Tip: treat this folder like OpenClaw’s “memory” and make it a git repo (ideally private) so your `AGENTS.md` + memory files are backed up. If git is installed, brand-new workspaces are auto-initialized.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/openclaw.md:83:Memory workflow: [Memory](/concepts/memory)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/openclaw.md:151:## Sessions and memory\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/lore.md:121:- npm packages released under new name\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/lore.md:159:- **memory/\\*.md** — The long-term memory files\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/hubs.md:47:- [Memory](/concepts/memory)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/hubs.md:160:- [macOS release](/platforms/mac/release)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/hubs.md:183:- [Research: memory](/experiments/research/memory)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/hubs.md:190:## Testing + release\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/providers/minimax.md:12:coding-focused release is **MiniMax M2.5** (December 23, 2025), built for\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/providers/minimax.md:15:Source: [MiniMax M2.5 release note](https://www.minimax.io/news/minimax-m25)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/providers/minimax.md:201:**2026.1.12** (unreleased at the time of writing). Fix by:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/providers/mistral.md:13:Mistral can also be used for memory embeddings (`memorySearch.provider = \"mistral\"`).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/lobster.md:208:(repeat daily, no memory of what was triaged)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/lobster.md:338:One public example: a “second brain” CLI + Lobster pipelines that manage three Markdown vaults (personal, partner, shared). The CLI emits JSON for stats, inbox listings, and stale scans; Lobster chains those commands into workflows like `weekly-review`, `inbox-triage`, `memory-consolidation`, and `shared-task-sync`, each with approval gates. AI handles judgment (categorization) when available and falls back to deterministic rules when not.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/chrome-extension.md:49:The extension ships inside the OpenClaw release (npm package) as static files. There is no separate “build” step.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/multi-agent-sandbox-tools.md:232:- `group:memory`: `memory_search`, `memory_get`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:180:`/debug` lets you set **runtime-only** config overrides (memory, not disk). Owner-only. Disabled by default; enable with `commands.debug: true`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:38:those to a prerelease, OpenClaw stops and asks you to opt in explicitly with a\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:39:prerelease tag such as `@beta`/`@rc` or an exact prerelease version.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:56:   selected for an exclusive slot such as memory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:91:- Memory (Core) — bundled memory search plugin (enabled by default via `plugins.slots.memory`)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:92:- Memory (LanceDB) — bundled long-term memory plugin (auto-recall/capture; set `plugins.slots.memory = \"memory-lancedb\"`)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:253:  `openclaw/plugin-sdk/mattermost`, `openclaw/plugin-sdk/memory-core`,\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:254:  `openclaw/plugin-sdk/memory-lancedb`,\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:342:- active memory slot plugin (default slot: `memory-core`)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:514:- `slots`: exclusive slot selectors such as `memory` and `contextEngine`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:548:      memory: \"memory-core\", // or \"none\" to disable memory plugins\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:557:- `memory`: active memory plugin (`\"none\"` disables memory plugins)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:560:If multiple plugins declare `kind: \"memory\"` or `kind: \"context-engine\"`, only\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:571:pipeline rather than just add memory search or hooks.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/index.md:40:- `coding`: `group:fs`, `group:runtime`, `group:sessions`, `group:memory`, `image`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/index.md:148:- `group:memory`: `memory_search`, `memory_get`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/clawhub.md:94:- **Versioning** with semver, changelogs, and tags (including `latest`).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/clawhub.md:169:- `--changelog <text>`: Changelog text (can be empty).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/clawhub.md:184:- `--changelog <text>`: Changelog for non-interactive updates.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/.i18n/README.md:8:- `<lang>.tm.jsonl` — translation memory (cache) keyed by workflow + model + text hash.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/.i18n/README.md:31:- The translation memory is updated by `scripts/docs-i18n`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/.i18n/zh-CN.tm.jsonl:474:{\"cache_key\":\"60cd1a8fee21c221c625fe6961c620592e9f99a88910d9f557d86f92e17d793c\",\"segment_id\":\"start/wizard.md:1d6bc09c9a9a3dad\",\"source_path\":\"start/wizard.md\",\"text_hash\":\"1d6bc09c9a9a3dad8fcbe9ed89a206b2dba3d8cf16046315aee976577d534cae\",\"text\":\"Downloads the appropriate release asset.\",\"translated\":\"下载相应的发布资源。\",\"provider\":\"pi\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5\",\"src_lang\":\"en\",\"tgt_lang\":\"zh-CN\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-01T13:47:59Z\"}\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/.i18n/zh-CN.tm.jsonl:676:{\"cache_key\":\"84e200d4c823802e34a99da4faa8328d0e250aca858b0a32cc08e3ae12e0cc0e\",\"segment_id\":\"start/wizard.md:e4442451c634e0db\",\"source_path\":\"start/wizard.md\",\"text_hash\":\"e4442451c634e0db2db0fae78725becbeafd567302e3ecbfeb5ccdc5887d29be\",\"text\":\" from GitHub releases:\",\"translated\":\" （从 GitHub 发布版本）：\",\"provider\":\"pi\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5\",\"src_lang\":\"en\",\"tgt_lang\":\"zh-CN\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-02-01T13:47:56Z\"}\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/session-pruning.md:11:Session pruning trims **old tool results** from the in-memory context right before each LLM call. It does **not** rewrite the on-disk session history (`*.jsonl`).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/session.md:179:OpenClaw trims **old tool results** from the in-memory context right before LLM calls by default.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/session.md:182:## Pre-compaction memory flush\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/session.md:184:When a session nears auto-compaction, OpenClaw can run a **silent memory flush**\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/session.md:186:the workspace is writable. See [Memory](/concepts/memory) and\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-loop.md:124:- On retry, in-memory buffers and tool summaries are reset to avoid duplicate output.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:12:file tools and for workspace context. Keep it private and treat it as memory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:69:  - Operating instructions for the agent and how it should use memory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:102:- `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:103:  - Daily memory log (one file per day).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:107:  - Curated long-term memory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:110:See [Memory](/concepts/memory) for the workflow and automatic memory flush.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:140:Treat the workspace as private memory. Put it in a **private** git repo so it is\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:154:git add AGENTS.md SOUL.md TOOLS.md IDENTITY.md USER.md HEARTBEAT.md memory/\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:198:git commit -m \"Update memory\"\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/context.md:20:Context is _not the same thing_ as “memory”: memory can be stored on disk and reloaded later; context is what’s inside the model’s current window.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/context.md:152:- **Pruning** removes old tool results from the _in-memory_ prompt for a run, but does not rewrite the transcript.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/compaction.md:66:Before compaction, OpenClaw can run a **silent memory flush** turn to store\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/compaction.md:67:durable notes to disk. See [Memory](/concepts/memory) for details and config.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/compaction.md:84:- **Session pruning**: trims old **tool results** only, **in-memory**, per request.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/system-prompt.md:62:- `MEMORY.md` and/or `memory.md` (when present in the workspace; either or both may be injected)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/system-prompt.md:69:> **Note:** `memory/*.md` daily files are **not** injected automatically. They\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/system-prompt.md:70:> are accessed on demand via the `memory_search` and `memory_get` tools, so they\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/presence.md:65:Presence entries are stored in a single in‑memory map:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/presence.md:81:This keeps the list fresh and avoids unbounded memory growth.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:3:summary: \"How OpenClaw memory works (workspace files + automatic memory flush)\"\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:5:  - You want the memory file layout and workflow\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:6:  - You want to tune the automatic pre-compaction memory flush\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:11:OpenClaw memory is **plain Markdown in the agent workspace**. The files are the\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:14:Memory search tools are provided by the active memory plugin (default:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:15:`memory-core`). Disable memory plugins with `plugins.slots.memory = \"none\"`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:19:The default workspace layout uses two memory layers:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:21:- `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:25:  - Curated long-term memory.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:35:- `memory_search` — semantic recall over indexed snippets.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:36:- `memory_get` — targeted read of a specific Markdown file/line range.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:38:`memory_get` now **degrades gracefully when a file doesn't exist** (for example,\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:44:## When to write memory\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:47:- Day-to-day notes and running context go to `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md:50:- If you want something to stick, **ask the bot to write it** into memory.","cwd":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773480350787}}
{"type":"message","id":"db13681c","parentId":"c564c9a9","timestamp":"2026-03-14T09:25:59.338Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Checking OpenClaw updates**\n\nI need to find out if the latest version of OpenClaw has memory added. It sounds like a good plan to check the documentation, especially the concepts and memory sections, along with the plugin docs. That should provide me with the most accurate and detailed information. Let’s get started on that and see what features have changed!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_06c197b4d2bab9340169b529a66fe8819194a6195bf5fac421\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABptSmpHg5aCnDl0BkFT2z8JN5AbU9oWBIwUp6uknyF5Uxty9m5ZPhwPdv1K2fsfkBZ-j24l7_qdrFRBYyeUbLE6hQWZovK1G61M8dH6KgCyn0ftd6ySxcNox4dh-YlgPKmyxwgeq1z8RTNI1UDhq_dZQFlIRolTmgLyP8ivoBNFCELGmTQKXqTS-OsXZd8ccP9BEzpFdRetg-E5cojOJhNIb6w3TEYmmRbRKp5KYXDE1hlFq3pqwnGxY1mlxwkRkVRqgHM1ktSORnSGzhRdjry9pbS6zd-PW9KQu41N6rVdl5tN797t3OXbtjEOPJdLu9EbuWSOK0gMo_yzS8LHFKkXy_8OkbQAK5AM8O4YeYXs2jNqYnQ_HuS-UUAbAxI8mkEYuW8ZaQeUr-AeufSHiNLsd3yFBzc5aHeq61zhmApH614qXlgxi-Dl_vYHWlEjRJwbolf06osgWjfrg9V8BGntJbjPVTtgJxZDAkMH6f8NDgjm9SDbGz9mZpanhVA9Zom3xmcJyhLvZY5gCygr3eqpFail-0q9zTVcBtfHjH6xXMmZ8i8NkjBH-ABpCAEeDQ8WbqW0P9OwGMdCZwi_V8R50TVulvrCzxrLETYt7tUilKT3rbgPh9Ja79WB6WPsesfBtis7U1Etm9QQzqAz-HEm9ZCUWhmr1Qoam3_lsBEjmW0KGz8cP7X2stzD65aGZRYH3pzOuNcQJmSLvVEU9YVC7zmOcItqXTPh1DxIG_3p17hdCLz1PQV3Y_n7TmRMYCiZ0Rd2iMnQHaKThB_BwaOKmFPEavSXaeZyl4kSqURcOOOt4caYUVpwcKbZix4-plTsh_3pqMAjyTRY-EGqK9eH31yvdp4hct1sBA2z5f8Km2B3BX0XCf67eMR0GfNy4q7HbyHRWvWeRzmaffgeRCMtWnnUo42nfoeYT7YbLLAAhcXVZ6WdslPef4xwaJRUl5VC7DVOPZiscCMsjAdSUpPaWGoPQ==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Checking OpenClaw updates**\\n\\nI need to find out if the latest version of OpenClaw has memory added. It sounds like a good plan to check the documentation, especially the concepts and memory sections, along with the plugin docs. That should provide me with the most accurate and detailed information. Let’s get started on that and see what features have changed!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_78fGSuui4GFOHcNU6eQhU7s1|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b529a9a9a88191b8b59bbb8ba89cbb","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md","offset":1,"limit":120},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/memory.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":120}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mKJVrvMDnkXUCYpJ3Mcjqbdo|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b529a9a9b4819196ef8271c02cbe26","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md","offset":88,"limit":20},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md\",\"offset\":88,\"limit\":20}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3Utk8KZLLbQCxPDaH1tCP8J7|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b529a9a9bc81919fdaaf6e84b088e2","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md","offset":283,"limit":40},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/session-management-compaction.md\",\"offset\":283,\"limit\":40}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":100978,"output":199,"cacheRead":21760,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":122937,"cost":{"input":0.25244500000000003,"output":0.0029850000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0054399999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.26087000000000005}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773480350793}}
{"type":"message","id":"7b6d614e","parentId":"db13681c","timestamp":"2026-03-14T09:25:59.349Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_78fGSuui4GFOHcNU6eQhU7s1|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b529a9a9a88191b8b59bbb8ba89cbb","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"Memory\"\nsummary: \"How OpenClaw memory works (workspace files + automatic memory flush)\"\nread_when:\n  - You want the memory file layout and workflow\n  - You want to tune the automatic pre-compaction memory flush\n---\n\n# Memory\n\nOpenClaw memory is **plain Markdown in the agent workspace**. The files are the\nsource of truth; the model only \"remembers\" what gets written to disk.\n\nMemory search tools are provided by the active memory plugin (default:\n`memory-core`). Disable memory plugins with `plugins.slots.memory = \"none\"`.\n\n## Memory files (Markdown)\n\nThe default workspace layout uses two memory layers:\n\n- `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`\n  - Daily log (append-only).\n  - Read today + yesterday at session start.\n- `MEMORY.md` (optional)\n  - Curated long-term memory.\n  - **Only load in the main, private session** (never in group contexts).\n\nThese files live under the workspace (`agents.defaults.workspace`, default\n`~/.openclaw/workspace`). See [Agent workspace](/concepts/agent-workspace) for the full layout.\n\n## Memory tools\n\nOpenClaw exposes two agent-facing tools for these Markdown files:\n\n- `memory_search` — semantic recall over indexed snippets.\n- `memory_get` — targeted read of a specific Markdown file/line range.\n\n`memory_get` now **degrades gracefully when a file doesn't exist** (for example,\ntoday's daily log before the first write). Both the builtin manager and the QMD\nbackend return `{ text: \"\", path }` instead of throwing `ENOENT`, so agents can\nhandle \"nothing recorded yet\" and continue their workflow without wrapping the\ntool call in try/catch logic.\n\n## When to write memory\n\n- Decisions, preferences, and durable facts go to `MEMORY.md`.\n- Day-to-day notes and running context go to `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.\n- If someone says \"remember this,\" write it down (do not keep it in RAM).\n- This area is still evolving. It helps to remind the model to store memories; it will know what to do.\n- If you want something to stick, **ask the bot to write it** into memory.\n\n## Automatic memory flush (pre-compaction ping)\n\nWhen a session is **close to auto-compaction**, OpenClaw triggers a **silent,\nagentic turn** that reminds the model to write durable memory **before** the\ncontext is compacted. The default prompts explicitly say the model _may reply_,\nbut usually `NO_REPLY` is the correct response so the user never sees this turn.\n\nThis is controlled by `agents.defaults.compaction.memoryFlush`:\n\n```json5\n{\n  agents: {\n    defaults: {\n      compaction: {\n        reserveTokensFloor: 20000,\n        memoryFlush: {\n          enabled: true,\n          softThresholdTokens: 4000,\n          systemPrompt: \"Session nearing compaction. Store durable memories now.\",\n          prompt: \"Write any lasting notes to memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md; reply with NO_REPLY if nothing to store.\",\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\nDetails:\n\n- **Soft threshold**: flush triggers when the session token estimate crosses\n  `contextWindow - reserveTokensFloor - softThresholdTokens`.\n- **Silent** by default: prompts include `NO_REPLY` so nothing is delivered.\n- **Two prompts**: a user prompt plus a system prompt append the reminder.\n- **One flush per compaction cycle** (tracked in `sessions.json`).\n- **Workspace must be writable**: if the session runs sandboxed with\n  `workspaceAccess: \"ro\"` or `\"none\"`, the flush is skipped.\n\nFor the full compaction lifecycle, see\n[Session management + compaction](/reference/session-management-compaction).\n\n## Vector memory search\n\nOpenClaw can build a small vector index over `MEMORY.md` and `memory/*.md` so\nsemantic queries can find related notes even when wording differs.\n\nDefaults:\n\n- Enabled by default.\n- Watches memory files for changes (debounced).\n- Configure memory search under `agents.defaults.memorySearch` (not top-level\n  `memorySearch`).\n- Uses remote embeddings by default. If `memorySearch.provider` is not set, OpenClaw auto-selects:\n  1. `local` if a `memorySearch.local.modelPath` is configured and the file exists.\n  2. `openai` if an OpenAI key can be resolved.\n  3. `gemini` if a Gemini key can be resolved.\n  4. `voyage` if a Voyage key can be resolved.\n  5. `mistral` if a Mistral key can be resolved.\n  6. Otherwise memory search stays disabled until configured.\n- Local mode uses node-llama-cpp and may require `pnpm approve-builds`.\n- Uses sqlite-vec (when available) to accelerate vector search inside SQLite.\n- `memorySearch.provider = \"ollama\"` is also supported for local/self-hosted\n  Ollama embeddings (`/api/embeddings`), but it is not auto-selected.\n\nRemote embeddings **require** an API key for the embedding provider. OpenClaw\nresolves keys from auth profiles, `models.providers.*.apiKey`, or environment\nvariables. Codex OAuth only covers chat/completions and does **not** satisfy\nembeddings for memory search. For Gemini, use `GEMINI_API_KEY` or\n`models.providers.google.apiKey`. For Voyage, use `VOYAGE_API_KEY` or\n`models.providers.voyage.apiKey`. For Mistral, use `MISTRAL_API_KEY` or\n\n[681 more lines in file. Use offset=121 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773480359343}}
{"type":"message","id":"a3c67dd7","parentId":"7b6d614e","timestamp":"2026-03-14T09:25:59.359Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_mKJVrvMDnkXUCYpJ3Mcjqbdo|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b529a9a9b4819196ef8271c02cbe26","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Available plugins (official)\n\n- Microsoft Teams is plugin-only as of 2026.1.15; install `@openclaw/msteams` if you use Teams.\n- Memory (Core) — bundled memory search plugin (enabled by default via `plugins.slots.memory`)\n- Memory (LanceDB) — bundled long-term memory plugin (auto-recall/capture; set `plugins.slots.memory = \"memory-lancedb\"`)\n- [Voice Call](/plugins/voice-call) — `@openclaw/voice-call`\n- [Zalo Personal](/plugins/zalouser) — `@openclaw/zalouser`\n- [Matrix](/channels/matrix) — `@openclaw/matrix`\n- [Nostr](/channels/nostr) — `@openclaw/nostr`\n- [Zalo](/channels/zalo) — `@openclaw/zalo`\n- [Microsoft Teams](/channels/msteams) — `@openclaw/msteams`\n- Google Antigravity OAuth (provider auth) — bundled as `google-antigravity-auth` (disabled by default)\n- Gemini CLI OAuth (provider auth) — bundled as `google-gemini-cli-auth` (disabled by default)\n- Qwen OAuth (provider auth) — bundled as `qwen-portal-auth` (disabled by default)\n- Copilot Proxy (provider auth) — local VS Code Copilot Proxy bridge; distinct from built-in `github-copilot` device login (bundled, disabled by default)\n\nOpenClaw plugins are **TypeScript modules** loaded at runtime via jiti. **Config\nvalidation does not execute plugin code**; it uses the plugin manifest and JSON\nSchema instead. See [Plugin manifest](/plugins/manifest).\n\n\n[1226 more lines in file. Use offset=108 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773480359353}}
{"type":"message","id":"80675374","parentId":"a3c67dd7","timestamp":"2026-03-14T09:25:59.380Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3Utk8KZLLbQCxPDaH1tCP8J7|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b529a9a9bc81919fdaaf6e84b088e2","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Pre-compaction “memory flush” (implemented)\n\nGoal: before auto-compaction happens, run a silent agentic turn that writes durable\nstate to disk (e.g. `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` in the agent workspace) so compaction can’t\nerase critical context.\n\nOpenClaw uses the **pre-threshold flush** approach:\n\n1. Monitor session context usage.\n2. When it crosses a “soft threshold” (below Pi’s compaction threshold), run a silent\n   “write memory now” directive to the agent.\n3. Use `NO_REPLY` so the user sees nothing.\n\nConfig (`agents.defaults.compaction.memoryFlush`):\n\n- `enabled` (default: `true`)\n- `softThresholdTokens` (default: `4000`)\n- `prompt` (user message for the flush turn)\n- `systemPrompt` (extra system prompt appended for the flush turn)\n\nNotes:\n\n- The default prompt/system prompt include a `NO_REPLY` hint to suppress delivery.\n- The flush runs once per compaction cycle (tracked in `sessions.json`).\n- The flush runs only for embedded Pi sessions (CLI backends skip it).\n- The flush is skipped when the session workspace is read-only (`workspaceAccess: \"ro\"` or `\"none\"`).\n- See [Memory](/concepts/memory) for the workspace file layout and write patterns.\n\nPi also exposes a `session_before_compact` hook in the extension API, but OpenClaw’s\nflush logic lives on the Gateway side today.\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting checklist\n\n- Session key wrong? Start with [/concepts/session](/concepts/session) and confirm the `sessionKey` in `/status`.\n- Store vs transcript mismatch? Confirm the Gateway host and the store path from `openclaw status`.\n- Compaction spam? Check:\n  - model context window (too small)\n  - compaction settings (`reserveTokens` too high for the model window can cause earlier compaction)\n\n[3 more lines in file. Use offset=323 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773480359371}}
{"type":"message","id":"ea81a9d0","parentId":"80675374","timestamp":"2026-03-14T09:26:28.040Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Clarifying updates and memory types**\n\nI need to provide a concise answer. I want to mention that there's an update available as of March 13, 2026, but it hasn't been installed yet. I'll also explain that OpenClaw memory refers to workspace markdown memory, which is different from Gemin-style proprietary memory. Keeping it clear and straightforward is crucial, so I'll make sure the explanation is easy to understand for the user.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_06c197b4d2bab9340169b529adb68c8191b8787a4c7bdf41b8\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABptSmw9oVqbjhveQ8x0RbzvvKkFYl07gX33zt7BH2eiizrOtyGBWLPAJ7QdmvPaLCpD_qn-d0ZJ3TM6VocHKZNgyLkMegGzmTNsxmfa6prTGAynEosWnqhImyWcRaaDZp4KWKLyHgeVnv6mBgoxYzG9TCXaWCZHdtCrHmN5Cvt4XBMDp3aBkD4lB2XGrTWV8lzigJ948P2vzKmjpdJ-dwXFtC4o5Y7pTQN6ZfmufimNkl2IXwVqqc8TWvLDWIGYQM4zVkLQIkKU3zSQh87QytKaSgrV1vBv0U3XqEnb8k4UAIKfiISj8jv-_n-UuMu3qeGCoBqdaPxSU4le7hRzTxikM-xslfEIXdKdlsmZfSzsQAOlRcpe2ITliDQGR5A1dHUJwwu15trYQSYF-v3wTU5iexZao641JqAcn7c-R9kA-EwV9zmkDJoN0qjwNupHoSKewClw8NYixoJYxoo6Nmy34wKFaL5wfWhcjpMsgaQujjMfwtEUhA-_m_-ZjpPo-5aqxZ8gjbMF1-Tw0ygOFTyx6FxSOqiZITcM7oW1c8hLdBnRdtp14LjB_oHjTUhr2lOHXtyjWVWt7tGjgiEebxim_hlpb4pXu8EMyVmbRnn551wdq8E4ltrORepCXQO9HL4f-0hRwovvCtIY7M8f8Ptcawd16ZL1DoM-X3OXitTwTK1sWtureh6yeUfp-UCO1Od3wZ8WADQkYrRos2xwMFeItIwRh05tHw5cnFk7PjU-6bowhu20TDpSVPNf3P6BcBCqK6zJbEMKdmheR2fqYY3Zj7DbsV_r86_6dASU5irvi0VnXWQtHViF7TaAbcTJhZ94rtiqDI1GHM6zanaXPwVMIGAnymNo8J3_vf75oHmu70dMqt5FQ4bN0GyHkBNTg3t0PRFEhr2IBMWPXIeXB0sJATr8qq7SwDr7K6wqe9rA_pZdOVrw9SBTc356YODFSWtBYljy11mSt6jZrCvvqrxHqBdj7jt50JqEQHGfaJhWqY0dVBNXpeGUbKlKUxyVUaz_EeAnckhPsRvsfFQe2ZQFPn65Q==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Clarifying updates and memory types**\\n\\nI need to provide a concise answer. I want to mention that there's an update available as of March 13, 2026, but it hasn't been installed yet. I'll also explain that OpenClaw memory refers to workspace markdown memory, which is different from Gemin-style proprietary memory. Keeping it clear and straightforward is crucial, so I'll make sure the explanation is easy to understand for the user.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 네. 확인해보니 **OpenClaw 최신 stable 업데이트가 available 상태**이고, 말씀하신 “메모리 기능”은 **Gemini식 사용자 프로필 메모리**보다는 **OpenClaw의 워크스페이스 기반 메모리 시스템**에 가깝습니다.\n\n## 현재 상태\n- 설치 채널: `stable`\n- 사용 가능 업데이트: **`2026.3.13`**\n- 상태 확인 결과: `openclaw update status` 에서 업데이트 가능 표시\n\n즉, **최신판에 메모리 관련 기능/정리가 들어가 있는 건 맞습니다.**\n\n---\n\n## OpenClaw 메모리의 의미\n\nOpenClaw 문서 기준으로 메모리는:\n\n> **agent workspace 안의 Markdown 파일이 source of truth**\n\n즉, 메모리를 DB에 숨겨서 쓰는 게 아니라, 기본적으로 **파일 기반 메모리**입니다.\n\n### 기본 구조\n- `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`\n  - 일일 로그\n  - append 중심\n- `MEMORY.md`\n  - 장기/정제된 기억\n  - durable facts, preferences, decisions\n\n이 구조는 지금 Sam workspace에서도 이미 쓰고 있는 방식과 일치합니다.\n\n---\n\n## 이번에 중요하게 볼 기능\n\n### 1) 자동 memory flush\n가장 실질적인 추가점은 이겁니다.\n\n세션이 **auto-compaction 직전**에 가면 OpenClaw가 조용히(silent turn):\n\n- “지금 남길 기억 있으면 파일에 써라”\n- 보통 `NO_REPLY`\n- 사용자에게 안 보이게 수행\n\n하는 **pre-compaction memory flush**를 돌릴 수 있습니다.\n\n문서상 기본값:\n- `agents.defaults.compaction.memoryFlush.enabled = true`\n- `softThresholdTokens = 4000`\n\n의미:\n- 컨텍스트가 잘리기 전에\n- 중요한 내용을 `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` 같은 파일에 남겨서\n- 세션 압축(compaction)으로 맥락 유실되는 걸 줄임\n\n이건 꽤 큽니다.  \n예전보다 **세션 지속성**이 좋아진다는 뜻입니다.\n\n---\n\n### 2) memory_search / memory_get\n에이전트가 메모리를 다루는 도구도 정리돼 있습니다.\n\n- `memory_search`\n  - 시맨틱 검색\n- `memory_get`\n  - 특정 메모리 파일/범위 읽기\n\n특히 `memory_get`은 이제 **파일이 없어도 graceful degrade** 하도록 문서화돼 있습니다.  \n즉 오늘 메모리 파일이 아직 없어도 에러로 죽지 않고 빈 결과로 처리 가능.\n\n운영 안정성 측면에서 좋은 변화입니다.\n\n---\n\n### 3) 벡터 기반 memory search\n문서상 OpenClaw는 `MEMORY.md` 와 `memory/*.md`에 대해 **semantic/vector memory search**를 지원합니다.\n\n자동 선택 가능 provider 예:\n- local\n- openai\n- gemini\n- voyage\n- mistral\n- ollama\n\n여기서 **Gemini는 “메모리 저장소”가 아니라 embeddings provider** 역할입니다.\n\n즉:\n- “Gemini memory가 OpenClaw에 추가됨”이라기보다\n- **OpenClaw memory search가 Gemini embeddings를 사용할 수 있음**\n- 혹은 memory 기능이 최신판에서 더 정식화/강화됨\n\n으로 이해하는 게 정확합니다.\n\n---\n\n## Gemini 메모리와 차이\n\n이 부분이 핵심입니다.\n\n### Gemini 메모리\n- 사용자 프로필/선호를 제품 내부에서 기억\n- SaaS형 persistent personalization\n\n### OpenClaw 메모리\n- **내 워크스페이스 파일에 기억을 저장**\n- 필요 시 검색/로드\n- compaction 전에 자동 flush 가능\n- 운영자 관점에서 **가시성, 감사성, 백업성**이 훨씬 좋음\n\nSam 같은 운영/보안 관점에서는 오히려 OpenClaw 방식이 더 마음 편할 수 있습니다.\n\n---\n\n## 보안/운영 관점 평가\n\n### 장점\n- **파일이 source of truth**라서 감사 가능\n- git/private backup 가능\n- memory lifecycle를 운영자가 통제 가능\n- hidden personalization보다 예측 가능\n- compaction 손실 완화\n\n### 주의점\n- 민감정보를 메모리 파일에 쓰면 그대로 남음\n- workspace 백업 정책이 잘못되면 유출면이 커짐\n- semantic memory provider를 remote embeddings로 쓰면 API 사용/비용/외부 전송 고려 필요\n\n즉:\n- **편의성은 증가**\n- 대신 **메모리 파일 자체를 민감자산처럼 관리**해야 함\n\n---\n\n## 한 줄 결론\n\n네, **OpenClaw 최신 버전에서 메모리 기능이 더 명확하게 들어가/정리된 건 맞습니다.**  \n다만 그 의미는 **Gemini처럼 앱 내부가 사용자를 기억하는 기능**이라기보다,\n\n- 워크스페이스 Markdown 메모리\n- semantic memory search\n- pre-compaction automatic memory flush\n\n를 갖춘 **운영 가능한 파일 기반 메모리 시스템**에 가깝습니다.\n\n원하시면 다음 중 하나로 이어서 해드릴게요:\n\n1. **Sam 환경 기준으로 이 기능이 지금 실제로 어떻게 동작하는지 점검**  \n2. `config`에서 **memoryFlush / memorySearch 설정 위치** 정확히 짚어드리기  \n3. **업데이트 전/후 영향도**를 운영 관점으로 정리  \n4. 바로 `openclaw update` 전에 **변경사항 검토 체크리스트** 만들어드리기","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_06c197b4d2bab9340169b529b0c7508191b2f32ade574fa119\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":95791,"output":1268,"cacheRead":28160,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":125219,"cost":{"input":0.2394775,"output":0.019020000000000002,"cacheRead":0.007039999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.2655375}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773480359375}}
{"type":"message","id":"8f3c2095","parentId":"ea81a9d0","timestamp":"2026-03-14T09:28:48.486Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"System: [2026-03-14 18:25:37 GMT+9] Exec completed (marine-f, code 0) :: (config) │ │ Update │ available · pnpm · npm update 2026.3.13 │ └──────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────…\n\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"1847\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"5487758242\",\n  \"sender\": \"Sam Yeo\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Sat 2026-03-14 18:28 GMT+9\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Sam Yeo (5487758242)\",\n  \"id\": \"5487758242\",\n  \"name\": \"Sam Yeo\",\n  \"username\": \"Lfantasial\"\n}\n```\n\n셋팅\n별도로 해야해?"}],"timestamp":1773480528480}}
{"type":"message","id":"e857ad84","parentId":"8f3c2095","timestamp":"2026-03-14T09:29:11.311Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_06c197b4d2bab9340169b52a56521c81919f806bfbfde32161\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABptSpXgy4lehY35VLfMH-SWGAWFxqAnAddEs-BZrbuuUfB-DbMxMJeIS8BgKrsk-vNCt4_VGfPBvXyJHKJiCB5oPS-qS4M7VKu05Dbanw9Pjp3Y1BdTLOZw2p9trYgtwILrF6LMwNw2n6lkbysfGk8ZqzgzV_n9ldkeDH6W0L9wQgBO2sQRPAdpqkZ8b_l88TNJKa5UvSGTNPn3ol24EOX_KvnnbndrLamFesp-U4vBWFf8g-dFfxImGK_w5e7deDsG_mT-ttVc7TBYlKzD3UYWklE6LJyaLxD6EgNoEd-q7fEUEKGJZBUe9-IvqQ1NgXCzJnA2kO8YTbVatlUT_4cWzbgo82ey9LGz6_40r9gzI_z1E82fjfAt-J7ZILsgGcSBbOLy9zYgGdKzoVxH-K75zBF6nUYHCCemkLGn0M_F--yWOmSsS9ehMmUSleuFob1MkiKBS5lymVuOYXGzn2_QV-EUEikyjE338u6pQuO_pLig79dI5oLgDKA5D2nyyiAzsWXWlNaowQvxV1h7_xfIfyC2AmoGk6uNaDHq13SW6_pmOctu6cI0zBMo8XJbAx-trlutSc-MC3GlKP_h2XESlnwLxczoAuq5aYURpAjAr4SKT_kaHzapRsuJ9uHpQekLB2R9_DNlanopWjXkqmeWJJ6is6qWzpF001HPAk8Di0M5-KPeW7OTulR8SFMm2y4yxRrKYDRtM0sbOj-xHpWB4XntaVU7pBdNQsJ6wikOPLs7MvB8IXw2ij1Xg0jbB1456Fto-orWGLwx9LbKbcdFv1ablf4UauwaRCL73hWJ9Q2ctHSOo_cUs1a_kLX302ZNGXETxJ2UfVDN2WtpOiCgZv5p1esf1w1RKDK6voSozX9RMo=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 네. **일부는 기본 동작**, 일부는 **별도 설정**이 필요합니다.\n\n## 결론 먼저\n\n### 별도 설정 없이 되는 것\n- 워크스페이스 파일 기반 메모리 자체\n  - `MEMORY.md`\n  - `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`\n- 메모리 파일을 읽고 쓰는 운영 방식\n- **pre-compaction memory flush** 기본 기능  \n  → 문서상 기본값은 `enabled: true`\n\n즉, **파일 메모리 + compaction 전 메모리 남기기**는 최신판에서 비교적 바로 활용 가능합니다.\n\n---\n\n### 별도 설정이 필요한 것\n다음은 따로 봐야 합니다.\n\n#### 1) semantic memory search\n즉, `memory_search`를 제대로 쓰는 벡터/임베딩 검색\n\n이건 provider 설정이 필요할 수 있습니다.\n\n예:\n- `agents.defaults.memorySearch.provider`\n- OpenAI / Gemini / Voyage / Mistral / Ollama / local 중 선택\n- remote provider면 API key 필요\n\n즉:\n- 그냥 Markdown 메모리만 쓸 거면 별도 설정 거의 불필요\n- **시맨틱 검색까지 제대로 쓸 거면 설정 필요**\n\n---\n\n#### 2) memory plugin slot 변경\n기본은 문서상:\n- `memory-core`\n\n선택적으로:\n- `memory-lancedb`\n\n이건 **플러그인 슬롯 변경 설정**이 필요합니다.\n\n---\n\n#### 3) Gemini를 memory provider로 쓰려는 경우\n이건 자동 저장 메모리 기능이 아니라,\n**embedding/search backend를 Gemini로 쓰는 설정**입니다.\n\n필요 항목:\n- `GEMINI_API_KEY` 또는\n- `models.providers.google.apiKey`\n\n즉, **Gemini 계정만 있다고 자동 연결되는 구조는 아님**.\n\n---\n\n## 실무적으로 보면\n\n### A. “그냥 메모리 파일 잘 쓰면 된다”\n이 경우:\n- 추가 설정 거의 없이 사용 가능\n- 지금 Sam workspace처럼 `MEMORY.md`, `memory/*.md` 운영하면 됨\n\n### B. “예전 대화/메모리를 의미 기반으로 잘 찾고 싶다”\n이 경우:\n- `memorySearch` 설정 필요\n- provider/API key/local model 선택 필요\n\n---\n\n## Sam 환경 기준 추천\n\n제 추천은 2단계입니다.\n\n### 1단계: 기본 파일 메모리 유지\n이미 하고 있는 방식 유지:\n- `MEMORY.md`\n- `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`\n\n이건 가장 안전하고 감사 가능.\n\n### 2단계: 필요하면 semantic search만 추가\n아래 조건이면 추가:\n- 메모리 양이 커짐\n- 과거 노트 검색이 잦음\n- session continuity 품질을 더 올리고 싶음\n\n그때:\n- local embeddings 우선 검토\n- 아니면 Gemini/OpenAI embeddings 연결\n\n---\n\n## 한 줄 답\n\n**네, 완전 자동은 아니고 용도에 따라 다릅니다.**  \n- **파일 메모리 + memory flush** → 거의 바로 사용 가능  \n- **semantic memory search / Gemini 연동** → 별도 설정 필요\n\n원하시면 제가 바로 다음 중 하나 해드릴게요:\n\n1. **현재 Sam OpenClaw 설정에서 memory 관련 항목이 이미 켜져 있는지 점검**  \n2. **Gemini 기반 memorySearch 설정 예시** 작성  \n3. **가장 안전한 운영 권장안(local vs remote)** 비교","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_06c197b4d2bab9340169b52a57d7e48191a484a0b0e28f8965\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":123666,"output":757,"cacheRead":21760,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":146183,"cost":{"input":0.309165,"output":0.011355,"cacheRead":0.0054399999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.32596}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773480528482}}
{"type":"message","id":"a2e0182e","parentId":"e857ad84","timestamp":"2026-03-14T09:29:34.415Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read HEARTBEAT.md if it exists (workspace context). Follow it strictly. Do not infer or repeat old tasks from prior chats. If nothing needs attention, reply HEARTBEAT_OK.\nWhen reading HEARTBEAT.md, use workspace file /home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/HEARTBEAT.md (exact case). Do not read docs/heartbeat.md.\nCurrent time: Saturday, March 14th, 2026 — 6:29 PM (Asia/Seoul) / 2026-03-14 09:29 UTC"}],"timestamp":1773480574409}}
{"type":"message","id":"22cfbcc2","parentId":"a2e0182e","timestamp":"2026-03-14T09:29:41.723Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_06c197b4d2bab9340169b52a879d3481919bb2e8122be34c31\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABptSqI0h2P-eFeOL6aRDTESyXLbIAiNvY7q9nJZjm0yB5xKeuTc1M4sDVHMEf3uN3X9XinIE87qoBD3y46LGxf-QcFzjG4LngBnid10n3UN3MfKvVn1XORECr5VsVzmwiMIoyuaGPG6whagR2R9-FGt8YmZ_WVpg_cAyo01-7DFDtIOjQS8p5oy7J39Q-nDlOtjtVQQHCr2EVQ_mAUtHfn0zdmvc3iID5ew0G4ixAxSUHLzcOEodi8qyIB6SdS-YnY_s25WqYbyLeUtnc0Wf-OgQEO1SPvP0VIrKaWm6l_4LmPBMbYUi23s9hI4MW1No_SueSoCPhlygytL7K4_-zUiKffBomrnC5ZQQWiRfQqvx1KNdYjFYOmMOyhMpLo6NQqkl_CbMO0nlDyxah2Pdtz1SGl7p8LisybsWSQUbkDdMuZlxe9x7fZj7cEH3yyNsi61pCR0D5QXhpvyHfM6WWlnfpGACmz9ITmIV6RToA0qvEopNBJsvhCXMOrueOEkf9rM32mOmMee9o-9fwpXUpko_Q7Cy0puJ-dE2Kx_bg4P4qxrv4pLVM-OpGWrmbrWBJHecJjXB8ydF0m5FG2oUBpPKx1fFpQJmOk8i7HMLaRs_J5gtMmgwgYUWMQuTgKU7ptyFOcT0f-PaFWnidlcH9Rx6gfBu2YtwK6qYP-geM0hwNmqZy7xN5EDO28JOCIxDQOm0X9BOZNYK5P9_5FsUQrpiNTnEbOk_WiVG0MAkph0DG0acrO7rbQFgO87_oGembdd6eNm5_WYhLIjDIOLwLIe7qkXJerk3NDkP3AV5JzoUTt5bzsK4SRynqMr8grQYRzWDGJF40fUHGPYKFrwYG_cG33AQ==\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8EmIjr4JFbwszZErVYHYrtWk|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b52a88d2048191b96204cb19225bcb","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"~/.agents/skills/using-superpowers/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.agents/skills/using-superpowers/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":145958,"output":40,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":145998,"cost":{"input":0.364895,"output":0.0006000000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.365495}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773480574411}}
{"type":"message","id":"b94b8d9e","parentId":"22cfbcc2","timestamp":"2026-03-14T09:29:41.733Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8EmIjr4JFbwszZErVYHYrtWk|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b52a88d2048191b96204cb19225bcb","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: using-superpowers\ndescription: Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring Skill tool invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions\n---\n\n<EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\nIf you think there is even a 1% chance a skill might apply to what you are doing, you ABSOLUTELY MUST invoke the skill.\n\nIF A SKILL APPLIES TO YOUR TASK, YOU DO NOT HAVE A CHOICE. YOU MUST USE IT.\n\nThis is not negotiable. This is not optional. You cannot rationalize your way out of this.\n</EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\n\n## How to Access Skills\n\n**In Claude Code:** Use the `Skill` tool. When you invoke a skill, its content is loaded and presented to you—follow it directly. Never use the Read tool on skill files.\n\n**In other environments:** Check your platform's documentation for how skills are loaded.\n\n# Using Skills\n\n## The Rule\n\n**Invoke relevant or requested skills BEFORE any response or action.** Even a 1% chance a skill might apply means that you should invoke the skill to check. If an invoked skill turns out to be wrong for the situation, you don't need to use it.\n\n```dot\ndigraph skill_flow {\n    \"User message received\" [shape=doublecircle];\n    \"About to EnterPlanMode?\" [shape=doublecircle];\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" [shape=box];\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Invoke Skill tool\" [shape=box];\n    \"Announce: 'Using [skill] to [purpose]'\" [shape=box];\n    \"Has checklist?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" [shape=box];\n    \"Follow skill exactly\" [shape=box];\n    \"Respond (including clarifications)\" [shape=doublecircle];\n\n    \"About to EnterPlanMode?\" -> \"Already brainstormed?\";\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" -> \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\";\n\n    \"User message received\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\";\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" -> \"Invoke Skill tool\" [label=\"yes, even 1%\"];\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" -> \"Respond (including clarifications)\" [label=\"definitely not\"];\n    \"Invoke Skill tool\" -> \"Announce: 'Using [skill] to [purpose]'\";\n    \"Announce: 'Using [skill] to [purpose]'\" -> \"Has checklist?\";\n    \"Has checklist?\" -> \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Has checklist?\" -> \"Follow skill exactly\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" -> \"Follow skill exactly\";\n}\n```\n\n## Red Flags\n\nThese thoughts mean STOP—you're rationalizing:\n\n| Thought | Reality |\n|---------|---------|\n| \"This is just a simple question\" | Questions are tasks. Check for skills. |\n| \"I need more context first\" | Skill check comes BEFORE clarifying questions. |\n| \"Let me explore the codebase first\" | Skills tell you HOW to explore. Check first. |\n| \"I can check git/files quickly\" | Files lack conversation context. Check for skills. |\n| \"Let me gather information first\" | Skills tell you HOW to gather information. |\n| \"This doesn't need a formal skill\" | If a skill exists, use it. |\n| \"I remember this skill\" | Skills evolve. Read current version. |\n| \"This doesn't count as a task\" | Action = task. Check for skills. |\n| \"The skill is overkill\" | Simple things become complex. Use it. |\n| \"I'll just do this one thing first\" | Check BEFORE doing anything. |\n| \"This feels productive\" | Undisciplined action wastes time. Skills prevent this. |\n| \"I know what that means\" | Knowing the concept ≠ using the skill. Invoke it. |\n\n## Skill Priority\n\nWhen multiple skills could apply, use this order:\n\n1. **Process skills first** (brainstorming, debugging) - these determine HOW to approach the task\n2. **Implementation skills second** (frontend-design, mcp-builder) - these guide execution\n\n\"Let's build X\" → brainstorming first, then implementation skills.\n\"Fix this bug\" → debugging first, then domain-specific skills.\n\n## Skill Types\n\n**Rigid** (TDD, debugging): Follow exactly. Don't adapt away discipline.\n\n**Flexible** (patterns): Adapt principles to context.\n\nThe skill itself tells you which.\n\n## User Instructions\n\nInstructions say WHAT, not HOW. \"Add X\" or \"Fix Y\" doesn't mean skip workflows.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773480581727}}
