{"type":"message","id":"cda13d0d","parentId":"f8f38b2b","timestamp":"2026-03-14T11:09:37.769Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f0399881919956a303c18f8f23\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABptUHxb9XLDtTc1Nv4R6yzByEeuMsIg6My8YXli3QBddxZZpwAAAa9gWXSWufWuHa6qqlVyW5ruHIEmMNGbdebOirYm_ezPhdYsIRBrCbLEmh_KTVp_eocqv-qx-3I-9Xmvnh6o8Ph7s_DT6OZix19AukErsYwhoTXYmiIpjD-cLt6blalU3r1YVMzqtHC_nCISo5X4-53xjBlu37lIxTc8bRhTczWUoLy_uqJvaCZFa1ZJFVWT8xpEgczsHGbPrBOAvShxA1Bq4tKmXN8sStYQdd2fTsNYEbmGYu02Fc2I8yHK7AGIfkW-EpogB4PdZGqBIsKKsXUIKwVqTUhDgNFQLU2qDi84ReROVnUiUx-B2TxWlzYxp0pofTA5G37XITBSTyMAOVZfT3xavj--TJkSnWWOz6teuX5Sg2_je0sdFF5FP1fFIwXCwjGuxBU64XbVvHNQQ38opDwKTU7Li3m56VOje-L0GN2cYV28otg3BbO2EW9bLCm0WUgPROvhiH4WLqr_JA4vYuPNj6YA7cvGO54GrMy5UK7rCSxI5-MjPiftF-ARFjp_GGub0TwrhvfLMWOEb7h34Yqg63RDkZOeJvUbShMm8x8IWIedsJatXqFAG4nUVZY-JwmI8Irwo7LgWnvjTjHJnjT-CaQyG9I9STZ8w4suKQ87HTVwN9DtQ8A_L1v8NnEe-QUCf3uCjxwwapV4s2_uQOeMqIr8qBcxUYZY7oSchDsX2-wz9sStPP4GFJmEobwxq0r09ejzxGGintQap17mqDrxIQ5hE8YCE80dCyS6p50bsD71aVmbLD_3TWi8OhEc-9_Yh8iaoY5oIzkaEBPln8bp3svfuwncXvbsg==\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ng8lssaUK3Wy1SjsbbxXgcwM|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f173e481919130f1ddb1303163","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"~/.agents/skills/using-superpowers/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.agents/skills/using-superpowers/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":150135,"output":40,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":150175,"cost":{"input":0.37533750000000005,"output":0.0006000000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.37593750000000004}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773486565807}}
{"type":"message","id":"3779f058","parentId":"cda13d0d","timestamp":"2026-03-14T11:09:37.788Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ng8lssaUK3Wy1SjsbbxXgcwM|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f173e481919130f1ddb1303163","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: using-superpowers\ndescription: Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring Skill tool invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions\n---\n\n<EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\nIf you think there is even a 1% chance a skill might apply to what you are doing, you ABSOLUTELY MUST invoke the skill.\n\nIF A SKILL APPLIES TO YOUR TASK, YOU DO NOT HAVE A CHOICE. YOU MUST USE IT.\n\nThis is not negotiable. This is not optional. You cannot rationalize your way out of this.\n</EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\n\n## How to Access Skills\n\n**In Claude Code:** Use the `Skill` tool. When you invoke a skill, its content is loaded and presented to you—follow it directly. Never use the Read tool on skill files.\n\n**In other environments:** Check your platform's documentation for how skills are loaded.\n\n# Using Skills\n\n## The Rule\n\n**Invoke relevant or requested skills BEFORE any response or action.** Even a 1% chance a skill might apply means that you should invoke the skill to check. If an invoked skill turns out to be wrong for the situation, you don't need to use it.\n\n```dot\ndigraph skill_flow {\n    \"User message received\" [shape=doublecircle];\n    \"About to EnterPlanMode?\" [shape=doublecircle];\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" [shape=box];\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Invoke Skill tool\" [shape=box];\n    \"Announce: 'Using [skill] to [purpose]'\" [shape=box];\n    \"Has checklist?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" [shape=box];\n    \"Follow skill exactly\" [shape=box];\n    \"Respond (including clarifications)\" [shape=doublecircle];\n\n    \"About to EnterPlanMode?\" -> \"Already brainstormed?\";\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" -> \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\";\n\n    \"User message received\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\";\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" -> \"Invoke Skill tool\" [label=\"yes, even 1%\"];\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" -> \"Respond (including clarifications)\" [label=\"definitely not\"];\n    \"Invoke Skill tool\" -> \"Announce: 'Using [skill] to [purpose]'\";\n    \"Announce: 'Using [skill] to [purpose]'\" -> \"Has checklist?\";\n    \"Has checklist?\" -> \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Has checklist?\" -> \"Follow skill exactly\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" -> \"Follow skill exactly\";\n}\n```\n\n## Red Flags\n\nThese thoughts mean STOP—you're rationalizing:\n\n| Thought | Reality |\n|---------|---------|\n| \"This is just a simple question\" | Questions are tasks. Check for skills. |\n| \"I need more context first\" | Skill check comes BEFORE clarifying questions. |\n| \"Let me explore the codebase first\" | Skills tell you HOW to explore. Check first. |\n| \"I can check git/files quickly\" | Files lack conversation context. Check for skills. |\n| \"Let me gather information first\" | Skills tell you HOW to gather information. |\n| \"This doesn't need a formal skill\" | If a skill exists, use it. |\n| \"I remember this skill\" | Skills evolve. Read current version. |\n| \"This doesn't count as a task\" | Action = task. Check for skills. |\n| \"The skill is overkill\" | Simple things become complex. Use it. |\n| \"I'll just do this one thing first\" | Check BEFORE doing anything. |\n| \"This feels productive\" | Undisciplined action wastes time. Skills prevent this. |\n| \"I know what that means\" | Knowing the concept ≠ using the skill. Invoke it. |\n\n## Skill Priority\n\nWhen multiple skills could apply, use this order:\n\n1. **Process skills first** (brainstorming, debugging) - these determine HOW to approach the task\n2. **Implementation skills second** (frontend-design, mcp-builder) - these guide execution\n\n\"Let's build X\" → brainstorming first, then implementation skills.\n\"Fix this bug\" → debugging first, then domain-specific skills.\n\n## Skill Types\n\n**Rigid** (TDD, debugging): Follow exactly. Don't adapt away discipline.\n\n**Flexible** (patterns): Adapt principles to context.\n\nThe skill itself tells you which.\n\n## User Instructions\n\nInstructions say WHAT, not HOW. \"Add X\" or \"Fix Y\" doesn't mean skip workflows.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773486577777}}
{"type":"message","id":"ead58a64","parentId":"3779f058","timestamp":"2026-03-14T11:09:44.981Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_eKF57gJ6paU99qqODXilHgpT|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f98fb481919141d4b5f1759bc8","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/HEARTBEAT.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/HEARTBEAT.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_zxYZA8WMHLPWLc4fXB4I8uTj|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f98fcc8191a294d272146191c1","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/SESSION-STATE.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/SESSION-STATE.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_wAuIGAgsyfzEkHtcFzd1TETe|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f98fd881918b49f6d1769c3f85","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/working-buffer.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/working-buffer.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9ZJG4P7gBLYMxcs0PJXTHK5r|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f98fdc8191a0e229fb1ba622d4","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/heartbeat-state.json"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/heartbeat-state.json\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_oiW7pI9X6pjxPLg5PczNtslH|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f98fe08191832f3c2980e24947","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-14.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-03-14.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_YTa3fu9bkx607BFnNnVIEucT|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f98fe88191bae672a4f1da69eb","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1186,"output":199,"cacheRead":150016,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":151401,"cost":{"input":0.002965,"output":0.0029850000000000002,"cacheRead":0.037503999999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.04345399999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773486577783}}
{"type":"message","id":"d3d717f5","parentId":"ead58a64","timestamp":"2026-03-14T11:09:44.994Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_eKF57gJ6paU99qqODXilHgpT|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f98fb481919141d4b5f1759bc8","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# HEARTBEAT.md\n\n## Sam heartbeat routine\n\nUse this file only for **isolated agentTurn** heartbeat jobs.\nThis file is not the general chat heartbeat rule. It is only for isolated cron/agentTurn heartbeat jobs, so the terminal response is `NO_REPLY`, not `HEARTBEAT_OK`.\nThis job must stay **small, deterministic, and quiet**.\n\n### Scope\nOnly read these files unless one is missing and must be created:\n- `SESSION-STATE.md`\n- `memory/working-buffer.md`\n- `memory/heartbeat-state.json`\n- today's `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`\n- `~/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json`\n\n### Meaningful finding\nTreat a finding as meaningful only when one of these is true:\n- a cron job newly entered a non-ok state\n- a cron job remains in a non-ok state\n- a cron job has `consecutiveErrors > 0`\n- `SESSION-STATE.md` contains an explicit blocker, risk, or open follow-up\n- the current heartbeat status materially differs from the last recorded state\n\nIf none of the above changed, update `memory/heartbeat-state.json` only.\n\n### State file format\nUse ISO8601 timestamps.\nStore `findings` as an array of short strings.\nKeep entries concise, operational, and stable across repeated runs.\n\n### Duplicate control\nDo not append the same finding to today's daily memory more than once unless the state materially changed.\nIf a cron error persists with no status change, keep the finding in `memory/heartbeat-state.json` but avoid repeating the same daily-memory bullet.\n\n### Do on each heartbeat\n1. Ensure these files exist:\n   - `SESSION-STATE.md`\n   - `memory/working-buffer.md`\n   - `memory/heartbeat-state.json`\n   - today's daily memory file\n2. Check only these conditions:\n   - any cron job with `lastStatus != ok`\n   - any cron job with `consecutiveErrors > 0`\n   - any explicit blocker/risk/follow-up already listed in `SESSION-STATE.md`\n3. Update `memory/heartbeat-state.json` with:\n   - `lastRunAt`\n   - `lastChecks.sessionState`\n   - `lastChecks.dailyMemory`\n   - `lastChecks.cron`\n   - `findings`\n4. If there is a meaningful finding:\n   - append one short operational bullet to today's daily memory file only if it is new or materially changed\n   - update `SESSION-STATE.md` only if priorities, blockers, or active follow-ups actually changed\n   - keep the finding concise and operational\n5. If nothing meaningful changed:\n   - update `memory/heartbeat-state.json` only\n6. Always finish with `NO_REPLY`\n\n### Guardrails\n- No proactive messages from this job\n- No external actions\n- No large rewrites\n- No secrets, tokens, passwords, cookies, or raw PII in any memory file\n- File memory remains the auditable source of truth\n- `claude-mem` remains semantic recall, not the policy source of truth\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773486584990}}
{"type":"message","id":"26e70de7","parentId":"d3d717f5","timestamp":"2026-03-14T11:09:45.010Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_zxYZA8WMHLPWLc4fXB4I8uTj|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f98fcc8191a294d272146191c1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SESSION-STATE.md\n\n**Updated:** 2026-03-14T09:06:00+09:00\n**Status:** active\n\n## Current focus\n- Memory baseline: `claude-mem` for semantic recall, file memory as auditable source of truth, proactive heartbeat for low-noise continuity.\n- Current task: keep local session-state aligned with current cron health and active priorities.\n\n## Active tasks\n- [x] Validate heartbeat state-file update path (manual verification completed)\n- [x] Reconfirm `github-repo-daily-briefing` cron health after the 2026-03-11 09:00 KST failure\n- [x] Confirm `workspace-heartbeat` timeout condition is cleared\n- [x] Refresh stale follow-up items in local state files when cron health changes\n\n## Decisions\n- `claude-mem` remains the primary semantic memory layer\n- `MEMORY.md` and `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` remain the durable file-memory system of record\n- Proactive automation should be quiet by default and only escalate meaningful findings\n\n## Risks / watch items\n- The proactive loop was previously only partially implemented\n- Avoid storing secrets, tokens, cookies, or raw PII in any memory layer\n- Prevent drift between semantic memory and file memory by treating file memory as policy/audit SoT\n\n## Next actions\n- Keep heartbeat quiet-by-default while tracking cron failures or state drift in local files\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773486585007}}
{"type":"message","id":"fee350d1","parentId":"26e70de7","timestamp":"2026-03-14T11:09:45.016Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_wAuIGAgsyfzEkHtcFzd1TETe|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f98fd881918b49f6d1769c3f85","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Working Buffer (Danger Zone Log)\n\n**Status:** INACTIVE\n**Started:** 2026-03-09T22:38:04+09:00\n**Activation Rule:** Start appending every exchange only when session context exceeds 60% or compaction risk is detected.\n\n---\n\n## Notes\n- Keep this file empty during normal operation.\n- When activated, append both the human message and a 1-2 sentence agent summary for each exchange.\n- After compaction/recovery, extract durable facts into `SESSION-STATE.md` or daily memory and then reset this file.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773486585014}}
{"type":"message","id":"7e2c7b7d","parentId":"fee350d1","timestamp":"2026-03-14T11:09:45.032Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_9ZJG4P7gBLYMxcs0PJXTHK5r|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f98fdc8191a0e229fb1ba622d4","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"lastRunAt\": \"2026-03-14T19:36:00+09:00\",\n  \"lastChecks\": {\n    \"sessionState\": \"2026-03-14T19:36:00+09:00\",\n    \"dailyMemory\": \"2026-03-14T19:36:00+09:00\",\n    \"cron\": \"2026-03-14T19:36:00+09:00\"\n  },\n  \"findings\": [\n    \"SESSION-STATE still carries risk/watch items about proactive loop maturity and file-memory drift control\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"file memory is the auditable source of truth; claude-mem remains semantic recall\"\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773486585029}}
{"type":"message","id":"1f6d965f","parentId":"7e2c7b7d","timestamp":"2026-03-14T11:09:45.044Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_oiW7pI9X6pjxPLg5PczNtslH|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f98fe08191832f3c2980e24947","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 2026-03-14\n\n- github-repo-daily-briefing cron remains in error state (consecutiveErrors=1, openai-codex auth refresh failure).\n- github-repo-daily-briefing cron recovered to ok at the 09:00 KST run; consecutiveErrors reset to 0.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773486585042}}
{"type":"message","id":"c21f095b","parentId":"1f6d965f","timestamp":"2026-03-14T11:09:45.064Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_YTa3fu9bkx607BFnNnVIEucT|fc_06c197b4d2bab9340169b541f98fe88191bae672a4f1da69eb","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"jobs\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"78f50a18-690a-4667-a12c-99a01398515c\",\n      \"agentId\": \"main\",\n      \"name\": \"daily-security-audit\",\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"notify\": true,\n      \"createdAtMs\": 1771254363238,\n      \"updatedAtMs\": 1773429205339,\n      \"schedule\": {\n        \"tz\": \"Asia/Seoul\",\n        \"expr\": \"0 3 * * *\",\n        \"kind\": \"cron\"\n      },\n      \"sessionTarget\": \"isolated\",\n      \"wakeMode\": \"now\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"message\": \"Run 'openclaw security audit --deep'. Ignore false positives from tavily-search (scripts/extract.mjs, scripts/search.mjs) and also from claude-mem (bun-runner.js, context-generator.cjs, mcp-server.cjs, smart-install.js, worker-cli.js) and writing-skills (render-graphs.js).\",\n        \"kind\": \"agentTurn\"\n      },\n      \"delivery\": {\n        \"mode\": \"announce\",\n        \"channel\": \"telegram\",\n        \"to\": \"telegram:5487758242\"\n      },\n      \"state\": {\n        \"nextRunAtMs\": 1773511200000,\n        \"lastRunAtMs\": 1773429174119,\n        \"lastStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDurationMs\": 31220,\n        \"consecutiveErrors\": 0,\n        \"lastRunStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDelivered\": true,\n        \"lastDeliveryStatus\": \"delivered\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dc1f52da-a247-4c7c-8ad8-c3f0d5ca71fc\",\n      \"agentId\": \"main\",\n      \"name\": \"daily-update-check\",\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"notify\": true,\n      \"createdAtMs\": 1771254363249,\n      \"updatedAtMs\": 1773435627366,\n      \"schedule\": {\n        \"tz\": \"Asia/Seoul\",\n        \"kind\": \"cron\",\n        \"expr\": \"0 6 * * *\"\n      },\n      \"sessionTarget\": \"isolated\",\n      \"wakeMode\": \"now\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"message\": \"Check for OpenClaw and skills updates using 'openclaw update status' and 'npx skills check'. If updates are available, verify that Telegram channel is synced and notify Sam with the update details.\",\n        \"kind\": \"agentTurn\"\n      },\n      \"delivery\": {\n        \"mode\": \"announce\",\n        \"channel\": \"telegram\",\n        \"to\": \"telegram:5487758242\"\n      },\n      \"state\": {\n        \"nextRunAtMs\": 1773522000000,\n        \"lastRunAtMs\": 1773435605860,\n        \"lastStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDurationMs\": 21506,\n        \"consecutiveErrors\": 0,\n        \"lastRunStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDelivered\": true,\n        \"lastDeliveryStatus\": \"delivered\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"07b6a467-2277-4376-8c4c-b8ae1a7ac74f\",\n      \"agentId\": \"main\",\n      \"name\": \"periodic-memory-maintenance\",\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"notify\": false,\n      \"createdAtMs\": 1771254363257,\n      \"updatedAtMs\": 1772978487686,\n      \"schedule\": {\n        \"expr\": \"0 23 * * 0\",\n        \"kind\": \"cron\",\n        \"tz\": \"Asia/Seoul\"\n      },\n      \"sessionTarget\": \"isolated\",\n      \"wakeMode\": \"now\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"kind\": \"agentTurn\",\n        \"message\": \"Read through recent memory files in 'workspace/memory/' and distill key learnings, decisions, and context into 'MEMORY.md'. Ensure the long-term memory remains curated and useful.\"\n      },\n      \"delivery\": {\n        \"mode\": \"announce\"\n      },\n      \"state\": {\n        \"nextRunAtMs\": 1773583200000,\n        \"lastRunAtMs\": 1772978403386,\n        \"lastStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDurationMs\": 84300,\n        \"consecutiveErrors\": 0,\n        \"lastRunStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDelivered\": true,\n        \"lastDeliveryStatus\": \"delivered\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"eb4407c8-7e9a-4d66-b956-2695d5aee260\",\n      \"agentId\": \"main\",\n      \"name\": \"daily-morning-briefing\",\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"notify\": true,\n      \"createdAtMs\": 1771254363268,\n      \"updatedAtMs\": 1773439235450,\n      \"schedule\": {\n        \"expr\": \"0 7 * * *\",\n        \"kind\": \"cron\",\n        \"tz\": \"Asia/Seoul\"\n      },\n      \"sessionTarget\": \"isolated\",\n      \"wakeMode\": \"now\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"kind\": \"agentTurn\",\n        \"message\": \"It's 7 AM. Provide a morning briefing for Sam: 1. Current weather in Seoul (using weather skill). 2. Brief system status overview. 3. Any urgent notifications or tasks from memory. Keep it sharp and helpful.\"\n      },\n      \"delivery\": {\n        \"mode\": \"announce\",\n        \"channel\": \"telegram\",\n        \"to\": \"telegram:5487758242\"\n      },\n      \"state\": {\n        \"nextRunAtMs\": 1773525600000,\n        \"lastRunAtMs\": 1773439202827,\n        \"lastStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDurationMs\": 32623,\n        \"consecutiveErrors\": 0,\n        \"lastRunStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDeliveryStatus\": \"delivered\",\n        \"lastDelivered\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"52ed00fd-cb4e-41ec-bde8-8c03c61c3d93\",\n      \"agentId\": \"main\",\n      \"sessionKey\": \"agent:main:main\",\n      \"name\": \"daily-github-backup\",\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"createdAtMs\": 1771408374779,\n      \"updatedAtMs\": 1773429287009,\n      \"schedule\": {\n        \"kind\": \"cron\",\n        \"tz\": \"Asia/Seoul\",\n        \"expr\": \"0 4 * * *\"\n      },\n      \"sessionTarget\": \"isolated\",\n      \"wakeMode\": \"now\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"message\": \"Execute the backup script at /home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/backup_to_github.sh using the exec tool. If it fails, report the error. If successful, simply confirm the backup is done.\",\n        \"kind\": \"agentTurn\"\n      },\n      \"delivery\": {\n        \"mode\": \"announce\",\n        \"channel\": \"telegram\",\n        \"to\": \"telegram:5487758242\"\n      },\n      \"state\": {\n        \"nextRunAtMs\": 1773514800000,\n        \"lastRunAtMs\": 1773429205339,\n        \"lastStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDurationMs\": 81670,\n        \"consecutiveErrors\": 0,\n        \"lastRunStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDelivered\": false,\n        \"lastDeliveryStatus\": \"not-delivered\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"de62862d-0431-460a-93d4-a21c9c54aa7c\",\n      \"agentId\": \"main\",\n      \"name\": \"notion-daily-briefing\",\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"createdAtMs\": 1772063184622,\n      \"updatedAtMs\": 1773442836224,\n      \"schedule\": {\n        \"kind\": \"cron\",\n        \"expr\": \"0 8 * * *\",\n        \"tz\": \"Asia/Seoul\"\n      },\n      \"sessionTarget\": \"isolated\",\n      \"wakeMode\": \"now\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"kind\": \"agentTurn\",\n        \"message\": \"Run 'python3 /home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/notion_daily_brief.py'. Then produce a concise Korean briefing for Sam: max 25 items (top priority first), include category counts and immediate actions. Keep under 3500 characters for Telegram delivery.\",\n        \"timeoutSeconds\": 300\n      },\n      \"delivery\": {\n        \"mode\": \"announce\",\n        \"channel\": \"telegram\",\n        \"to\": \"telegram:5487758242\"\n      },\n      \"state\": {\n        \"nextRunAtMs\": 1773529200000,\n        \"lastRunAtMs\": 1773442802929,\n        \"lastRunStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDurationMs\": 33295,\n        \"lastDelivered\": true,\n        \"lastDeliveryStatus\": \"delivered\",\n        \"consecutiveErrors\": 0\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0f2e06c5-425c-40b2-845b-135e47277fe1\",\n      \"name\": \"github-repo-daily-briefing\",\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"createdAtMs\": 1772414390336,\n      \"updatedAtMs\": 1773446484176,\n      \"schedule\": {\n        \"kind\": \"cron\",\n        \"expr\": \"0 9 * * *\",\n        \"tz\": \"Asia/Seoul\"\n      },\n      \"sessionTarget\": \"isolated\",\n      \"wakeMode\": \"now\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"kind\": \"agentTurn\",\n        \"message\": \"매일 09:00 KST 기준으로 GitHub 인기 레포 브리핑을 생성해 Sam에게 한국어로 전달하세요. 반드시 GitHub API(gh api 또는 공식 REST)로 실제 데이터를 조회하세요. 출력 형식: (1) 최근 인기 Top 5(최근 7일 생성 + stars 기준), (2) 누적 스타 상위 Top 5(archived 제외, 가능하면 최근 활동 있는 레포 우선), (3) 각 레포 핵심 설명 1~2문장(무엇/왜 중요한지), (4) OpenClaw 또는 Claude Code에 바로 적용 가능한 아이디어 3~5개(자동화/보안/개발생산성 관점), (5) 오늘 바로 실행할 액션 3개. 중복 레포는 한 번만 노출하고 전체 2500자 이내로 간결하게 작성하세요.\",\n        \"timeoutSeconds\": 300\n      },\n      \"delivery\": {\n        \"mode\": \"announce\",\n        \"channel\": \"telegram\",\n        \"to\": \"telegram:5487758242\"\n      },\n      \"state\": {\n        \"nextRunAtMs\": 1773532800000,\n        \"lastRunAtMs\": 1773446402804,\n        \"lastRunStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDurationMs\": 81372,\n        \"lastDeliveryStatus\": \"delivered\",\n        \"consecutiveErrors\": 0,\n        \"lastDelivered\": true\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"34ae8346-6001-49dd-b83d-17865b2b46c3\",\n      \"name\": \"workspace-heartbeat\",\n      \"description\": \"Low-noise workspace heartbeat for session state, cron health, and file-memory continuity\",\n      \"enabled\": true,\n      \"createdAtMs\": 1773063542846,\n      \"updatedAtMs\": 1773478836910,\n      \"schedule\": {\n        \"kind\": \"cron\",\n        \"expr\": \"0 9,12,15,18,21 * * *\",\n        \"tz\": \"Asia/Seoul\"\n      },\n      \"sessionTarget\": \"main\",\n      \"wakeMode\": \"now\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"kind\": \"systemEvent\",\n        \"text\": \"Read HEARTBEAT.md if it exists (workspace context). Follow it strictly. Do not infer or repeat old tasks from prior chats. If nothing needs attention, reply HEARTBEAT_OK.\"\n      },\n      \"state\": {\n        \"nextRunAtMs\": 1773489600000,\n        \"lastRunAtMs\": 1773478803593,\n        \"lastRunStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastStatus\": \"ok\",\n        \"lastDurationMs\": 33317,\n        \"lastDeliveryStatus\": \"not-requested\",\n        \"consecutiveErrors\": 0\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773486585056}}
